      },
      "id": "b04b006c-132f-41f9-9046-6eb2f867feb8",
      "name": "Record Contact Failure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2860,
        600
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Draft-only outreach\nSelect Supabase, OpenRouter and Gmail credentials. New/qualified contacts with no outreach_drafted_at are eligible. Pass contact_ids as a JSON UUID array to scope a manager run; empty array intentionally selects nobody. The loop processes one contact at a time and reports partial failures.\nA successful Gmail draft is recorded on the contact so later runs skip it. Avoid overlapping runs: Gmail and Postgres are separate services and cannot share a transaction. If Gmail succeeds but saving the receipt fails (or a request times out), inspect Gmail and reconcile the receipt before retrying. No automatic mutation retries are configured.",
        "width": 1080,
        "height": 300
      },
      "id": "f872c4d8-9de3-4e97-b29d-1bedb8da2b38",
      "name": "Setup and Operating Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        950
      ]
    }
